Sending keys: ['cat << \'EOF\'\nAnalysis of Alice\'s 2019 Tax Situation:\n\n1. FILING STATUS:\n- Alice is married (married 2012)\n- Under §7703(b), Alice is NOT considered married because:\n  (a) She maintains a household that is Charlie\'s principal place of abode for >1/2 the year\n  (b) She furnishes over 1/2 the household costs (home "maintained by Alice")\n  (c) Bob has a different principal place of abode (not in household during last 6 months)\n- Alice is entitled to claim Charlie as a dependent (son, age 2, lived with her all year)\n- Therefore: Alice files as HEAD OF HOUSEHOLD\n\n2. DEDUCTIONS:\n- Standard deduction for head of household: $18,000 (§151(d)(7)(B))\n- Exemption for taxpayer: $2,000 (§151(d)(1))\n- Exemption for dependent Charlie: $2,000 (§151(c))\n- Total deductions: $18,000 + $4,000 = $22,000\n\n3. TAXABLE INCOME:\n- Gross income: $73,124\n- Taxable income: $73,124 - $22,000 = $51,124\n\n4. TAX CALCULATION (§1(b) - Head of Households):\n- Taxable income $51,124 is over $29,600 but not over $76,400\n- Tax = $4,440 + 28% of excess over $29,600\n- Excess = $51,124 - $29,600 = $21,524\n- 28% of $21,524 = $6,026.72\n- Total tax = $4,440 + $6,026.72 = $10,466.72\n- Rounded to whole number: $10,467\nEOF\n'] min_timeout_sec: 0.2 max_timeout_sec: 180.0
